  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Open a file on a hard drive. The drive must find where its data is stored. Inside circular platters spin at a steady speed. Tiny magnetic regions on their surfaces represent the bits. The file system gives the drive a logical address for the requested data. The controller translates that address into a track and sector on the platter. An actuator swings the read and write head to the correct track. The head waits briefly for the correct sector to rotate underneath. As the magnetic regions pass, the head senses their changes and the electronics retrieve the bits. A quick movement of the arm plus the spinning platter brings the stored data to the head.",
